---
import Page from "../layouts/page.astro";
import { supportEmail } from "../site";

// Follows docs/legal/terms.md. Change both together.
const updated = "November 9, 2026";
---

<Page
  title="Terms of use · Ourio"
  description="The terms for using Ourio, the iPhone app for couples: your account, what you send, coins, ending your account and our limits."
>
  <article class="container-page pt-10 pb-24 md:pt-14">
    <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-[18ch] text-h2">Ourio terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[40rem] text-lead text-soft">
      Ourio is a private app for two people to send each other drawings and photos, and to share a cat, a room and small
      games. By using the app you accept these terms.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-small text-muted">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-09">{updated}</time></p>

    <div class="doc">
      <h2 id="account">Your account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The app creates an anonymous account for you. Keep your iCloud Keychain, or link Sign in with Apple in the app, if
          you want a new phone to find your account.
        </li>
        <li>
          You must be at least 13. If you are under the age of majority where you live, you need a parent's or guardian's
          permission.
        </li>
        <li>
          You are responsible for who you share your invite code with. Anyone with a valid code can become your partner until
          you unpair.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="content">What you send</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your drawings, photos and words are yours. You give us the right to store them and show them to your partner so the
          app works, and nothing else. We don't sell them, use them for ads, or train AI on them (see the{" "}
          <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Don't send anything unlawful, abusive or that you have no right to send. We may remove content or close an account
          that breaks this, or to protect people. You can report or block your partner in Settings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="coins">Coins</h2>
      <p>
        Coins are earned in the app and have no cash value. They can't be exchanged, transferred outside your pair or
        refunded for money.
      </p>

      <h2 id="use">Using the app</h2>
      <p>
        Don't copy or reverse engineer the app, attack the service, or use it to send spam or to harass anyone. We may change
        or stop features, for example the games or the shop, and will try to give notice for changes that remove your data.
      </p>

      <h2 id="ending">Ending</h2>
      <p>
        You can unpair or delete your account at any time in Settings. We may suspend an account that breaks these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 id="limits">No promises</h2>
      <p>
        Ourio is provided as is. We work to keep it available and your notes safe, but we can't promise it will never be down
        or lose data. To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for indirect loss. Nothing here limits rights you have by
        law as a consumer.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        We may change these terms and will change the date above. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}
          >{supportEmail}</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Page>
